                                    <h1>Amazon Ads + ACOS Benchmarks India 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Amazon India drives 30-70% of category volume for many D2C brands. Amazon Advertising is now a serious spend for scaling brands — often 8-18% of Amazon revenue. Here are real 2026-2027 CPC + ACOS benchmarks based on 200+ Amazon accounts we've operated.</p>
                                    <h2>Amazon Sponsored Products CPC by Category (India 2026)</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Beauty / cosmetics:</strong> ₹6-24.<br><strong>Fashion:</strong> ₹4-16.<br><strong>Home &amp; kitchen:</strong> ₹5-20.<br><strong>Consumer electronics:</strong> ₹8-32 (high competitor bidding).<br><strong>Grocery / F&amp;B:</strong> ₹3-12.<br><strong>Wellness / supplements:</strong> ₹7-24.<br><strong>Books:</strong> ₹1-4 (cheapest).<br><strong>Baby care + kids:</strong> ₹5-18.</p>
                                    <h2>ACOS Benchmarks</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Scaling brands:</strong> 20-35% ACOS.<br><strong>Optimised brands:</strong> 12-22% ACOS.<br><strong>Break-even (depends on margin):</strong> typically 30-45% ACOS for most categories.<br><strong>Below break-even:</strong> losing money per order — investment mode only.<br>TACOS (Total ACOS including organic sales): 5-15% typical for well-optimised brands.</p>
                                    <h2>Sponsored Brands + Sponsored Display</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Sponsored Brands (formerly headline search):</strong> higher CPC (₹15-60) but drives brand awareness + Store visits.<br><strong>Sponsored Display:</strong> off-Amazon + retargeting. Lower CPM (₹80-250) but weaker attribution.<br><strong>Sponsored Video:</strong> premium video placements. ₹300-1,200 CPM.<br>For growth-stage: 60-75% Sponsored Products + 15-25% Sponsored Brands + 5-15% Sponsored Display typical mix.</p>
                                    <h2>Amazon Advertising Best Practices 2026</h2>
                                    <p>1. <strong>Catalog optimisation is primary lever</strong> — titles, images (7+), A+/EBC content, videos.<br>2. <strong>Keyword bid tiering</strong> — brand + high-intent + long-tail different bid strategies.<br>3. <strong>Negative keyword hygiene</strong> — regular exclusion of irrelevant queries.<br>4. <strong>Product Targeting</strong> ads — compete for competitor PDPs.<br>5. <strong>Amazon Live + posts</strong> — free organic brand awareness.<br>6. <strong>Subscribe &amp; Save</strong> — subscription-adjacent Amazon feature. Lifts LTV.<br>7. <strong>Deal timing</strong> — Prime Day + Great Indian Festival + Diwali sale peaks.</p>
                                    <h2>Amazon vs Flipkart India Ads</h2>
                                    <p>Amazon India dominates most categories except select verticals where Flipkart is stronger (large appliances, some fashion sub-categories, Big Billion Days shoppers).<br><strong>Amazon India ad spend:</strong> 8-18% of Amazon revenue typical.<br><strong>Flipkart ad spend:</strong> 6-14% of Flipkart revenue typical.<br><strong>Both:</strong> essential for volume + discovery. Reserve premium collections for brand.com.</p>
                                    <h2>Amazon Business Marketing</h2>
                                    <p>Amazon Business (B2B marketplace) underrated — bulk orders + higher AOV + reseller / distributor discovery. Ad spend 4-10% of B2B revenue for brands with B2B potential.</p>

